# The annotations of demo: the source of src/demo/*.asm (../../kit/mkgame.py --part src/demo/demo.json). Format:
# ../../../../docs/ann-format.md.
@equ $5B60 Temp1 2 ; scratch and inputs
@equ $5B62 Temp2 2 ; 
@equ $5B64 Temp3 2 ; 
@equ $5B66 Temp4 2 ; 
@equ $5B6C BoxAttr ; PrintBoxed: the box's attribute
@equ $5B6E RandomSeed 2 ; Random $C6CE's seed
@equ $5B70 RandomSeed2 ; Random2 $9E6A's seed
@equ $5B71 DigitTemp 2 ; ToDigits $9EE8's work
@equ $5B73 Digits 5 ; ToDigits $9EE8's five digits, units first
@equ $5B7B ControlXor ; XORed with every port read: 0 keys, $FF Kempston
@equ $5B7C SpriteX ; DrawSprite: X in pixels
@equ $5B7D SpriteY ; Y in lines
@equ $5B7E SpriteWidth ; width in bytes
@equ $5B7F SpriteHeight ; height in lines
@equ $5B80 RexFrame ; Rex's walking frame
@equ $5B83 RexX ; Rex: X in pixels
@equ $5B84 RexY ; Y in lines
@equ $5B85 Room ; the room Rex is in
@equ $5B86 RoomColumn ; DrawRoom's column
@equ $5B88 RexFacing ; 0 right, 1 left
@equ $5B89 FallSpeed ; Rex's fall speed
@equ $5B8A Jumping ; Rex is jumping
@equ $5B8D JumpPtr 2 ; the jump's step in JumpSteps $D3C8
@equ $5B8F RexSpeed ; Rex's sideways speed
@equ $5B90 ObjectCount ; the room's object records (its list's first byte & $1F)
@equ $5B91 RoomRight ; the room's exits (RoomExits $B033): right
@equ $5B92 RoomUp ; up
@equ $5B93 RoomDown ; down
@equ $5B94 RoomLeft ; left
@equ $5E9B FireLatch ; 1 while fire is held (one shot a press for the slow weapons)
@equ $5E9C Weapon ; the weapon in use: 0 gun, 1 double fire, 2 laser, 3 multiple (drones), 4 spray
@equ $5E9D PowerLevel ; the weapon's power, 1-6 (the power bar)
@equ $5E9E PowerBarPtr 2 ; the HUD address of the power bar's end
@equ $5EA0 PassToggle ; flips every pass (the animations run every other pass)
@equ $5EA1 PowerCount ; power pods towards the next power level
@equ $5EA2 RexCellPtr 2 ; Rex's place in the room grid (CellPointer $9FD7)
@equ $5EA4 ObjectCellPtr 2 ; the current object's place in the grid (ObjectCell $CCF8)
@equ $5EA6 RoomCellPtr 2 ; DrawRoom's grid pointer
@equ $5EA9 ObjectListPtr 2 ; the room's object list (RoomObjectLists)
@equ $5EB1 BoxX ; PrintBoxed: the box's column
@equ $5EB2 BoxY ; PrintBoxed: the box's line
@equ $5EB3 BoxWidth ; PrintBoxed: the box's width
@equ $5EB4 BoxHeight ; PrintBoxed: the box's height
@equ $5EB5 SpawnLeft ; the room spawns from the left
@equ $5EB6 SpawnRight ; the room spawns from the right
@equ $5EB7 SpawnTop ; the room spawns from the top
@equ $5EB8 SmartBombSteps ; the smart bomb's steps left (16)
@equ $5EB9 SmartBombOn ; a smart bomb runs
@equ $5EBA SmartBombPtr 2 ; the next object to kill
@equ $5EBC SpriteMirror ; DrawSprite: bit 7 a fixed frame, SpritePicture, the frame list ignored (mirroring, through MirrorTable $AE0E, is A not 0 at the call)
@equ $5EBD SpritePicture 2 ; DrawSprite: the picture
@equ $5EBF ArrowPathPtr 2 ; the tutor arrow's place in ArrowPath (TutorArrow)
@equ $5EC1 ArrowMoving ; the arrow moves along its path (0: held at the start)
@equ $5EC2 KillFlashPtr 2 ; the combo row cell lit by the latest hit (REX 1's; DEMO keeps no combo)
@equ $5EC4 ComboCount ; kills in a row
@equ $5EC5 ComboTimer ; passes left for the next kill to count in the row
@equ $5EC7 Score 2 ; the score, in hundreds
@equ $5EC9 RapidShotsOn ; the 100 RAPID SHOTS bonus runs
@equ $5ECA RapidShotsLeft ; its shots left
@equ $5ECB FadeStepIndex ; the power pod's HUD flash step, $FF at rest (FadeStep $9A4C)
@equ $5ECC SpawnTimer ; passes to the next random spawn
@equ $5ECD SpawnPeriod ; the room's spawn period
@equ $5ECE ScriptSpawnStep ; the scripted spawn's step (ScriptSpawn $A9F4), 0 off
@equ $5ECF ScriptSpawnTimer ; passes to the next scripted spawn
@equ $5ED1 ScriptSpawnCount ; scripted spawns made
@equ $5ED2 ShieldOn ; the shield is on
@equ $5ED5 ShieldKeyLatch ; the down key is held (one toggle a press)
@equ $5ED6 ShieldEnergy ; the shield's energy, 0-99
@equ $5ED7 ShieldDrainRate ; passes for one unit of energy while the shield is on
@equ $5ED8 WeaponIcon ; the gun held (always 1): BestWeapon reads it as entry 0 before HasDoubleFire .. HasSpray
@equ $5ED9 HasDoubleFire ; the weapons held: double fire
@equ $5EDA HasLaser ; laser
@equ $5EDB HasMultiple ; multiple (drones)
@equ $5EDC HasSpray ; spray
@equ $5EDD EnemyShotKind ; the kind of the next enemy bullet
@equ $5EDE Dying ; Rex is dying
@equ $5EDF DeathTimer ; the death animation's passes left
@equ $5EE0 DeathShardPtr 2 ; the shards' path pointer
@equ $5EE2 RestartX ; the restart point: X
@equ $5EE3 RestartY ; Y
@equ $5EE4 RestartRoom ; room
@equ $5EE5 RestartFacing ; facing
@equ $5EE6 RexPresent ; 1 when Rex is fully there (he moves and fires), 0 while he materialises or after he vanished
@equ $5EE7 SparkleCount ; the sparkle's cell mask step (18 to 0 in, 0 to 18 out)
@equ $5EE8 SparkleOn ; the sparkle's dots run
@equ $5EE9 SparkleMode ; the sparkle is shown
@equ $5EEA SparkleTimer ; the dots' passes left
@equ $5EEB Vanishing ; 1: the sparkle takes Rex out (a death), 0: it brings him in
@equ $5EEC Lives ; lives left (4 at the start, up to 9)
@equ $5EED SweepPos ; the HUD sweep's position
@equ $5EEE SweepCount ; sweeps made at this width
@equ $5EEF SweepDir ; the sweep's direction
@equ $5EF0 SweepWidth ; the sweep's width (12 after ResetSweep; Rex dies when it would drop to 0)
@equ $5EF1 FireDelay ; passes between shots
@equ $5EF2 AnimCount1 ; animation counters of the cells
@equ $5EF3 AnimCount2 ; 
@equ $5EF4 AnimCount3 ; 
@equ $5EF5 Bombs ; smart bombs left
@equ $5EF6 ObjectTable ; the room's object records, 23 bytes each (UpdateObjects, SmartBombMark)
@equ $6067 WeaponRank ; the best weapon held
@equ $6068 BonusRoll ; the bonus roulette's position
@equ $606A Immune ; Rex cannot die (never set)
@equ $606B SpeedUp ; the SPEED UP bonus: passes left
@equ $606C SpeedUpPhase ; 
@equ $606F ExtraLifeCount 2 ; hundreds of points towards the next life
@equ $6071 HeatColour ; the colour of the HUD cell $5817 (ShowHeat): 7 at a death, + 1 every 100 passes (HeatStep)
@equ $6072 HeatCount 2 ; passes to the next HeatStep
@equ $6074 OnLift ; Rex stands on a ladder or lift
@equ $6075 ShotSide ; FindShotSlot: 0 Rex's bullets, 1 the enemies'
@equ $6076 AnimCount4 ; the animated cells' counter (AnimateCells)
@equ $6077 BonusDelay 2 ; the bonus roulette's step count, smaller each step
@equ $6079 TutorInput ; the input the script holds now, bits low = pressed: 0 fire, 1 up, 2 down, 3 right, 4 left
@equ $607F TutorUnused ; set to 0 by TutorReset, never read
@equ $6080 TutorScriptPtr 2 ; the [input][count] pair in play
@equ $6082 TutorCount ; passes left on this pair
@equ $6083 TutorFrame 2 ; passes since the room's tutor began (the panels' clock)
@equ $6085 TutorRoomPtr 2 ; the next room in TutorRooms $A2A2
@equ $6087 TutorDone ; room 2's tutor shown
@alias ShadowOffset $E4FF-$5800 ; the distance from a screen attribute to its cell in the attribute shadow $E4FF (PowerBar adds it); not an address in the sprites
@isub $C287 LD DE,ShadowOffset

@module graphics ; The development link, the graphics and the level data: the font, the characters, the blocks, the room maps and the sprites
@about DEMO's code block loads at $61A8 like part 2's, and its first 314 bytes are part 2's development link byte for byte but the return address word $62BE ($DB4B here). The graphics follow part 1's at +$258 (font, characters, blocks); the sprites are part 1's set without the roll call and with the tutor's arrow ($88FC).
$61A8 b DevLink 16 ; Leftover: the development link's code, part 2's own (DevLink in src/rex2/graphics.asm): pages the link in, saves every register, then serves the host's commands until a return
> Byte for byte part 2's but the word at $62BE (the return address the host's command $B5 sets: $DB4B in DEMO, $D6C6 in REX 2). Nothing calls it.
@res leftovers/demo-devlink.bin
$62C3 DevLinkGet ; code: E = a byte from the host (port $1F) after the handshake on port $3F
$62D3 DevLinkPut ; code: a byte to the host (port $1F), then the handshake on port $3F
$62E2 b DevLinkState 8 ; The link's state: a work word, the 26 bytes it sends ($62E4), the saved HL, return address and SP; tape garbage, never written in play
@res leftovers/demo-devlink.bin
$62FE b Unused62FE 8 ; Leftover: 58 zero bytes before the font (its codes 25-31 would be at $6300-$6337); nothing reads them
@res leftovers/demo-devlink.bin
$6338 b Font 8 ; The font: 64 characters, codes 32-95 (space to underscore), 8 bytes each, at $6238 + 8 x code
> PrintChar, PrintDigits and the box frame of PrintBoxed read it.
@res fonts/demo.bin
$6538 b CharFlags 16 ; The cell type of each of the 256 room characters: what Rex and the objects test in the room grid
> DrawRoomCell copies CharFlags[c] into the grid for each character drawn; the types are part 1's.
@res tables/demo-char-flags.bin
$6638 b CharGraphics 8 ; The 256 room characters, 8 bytes each
@res chars/demo.bin
$6690 AnimChar11 ; character 11, rolled one line up by RollCharUp every pass (the main loop)
$6708 AnimChar26 ; character 26, rolled one line down by RollCharDown
$6718 AnimChar28 ; character 28, rolled one line down by RollCharDown
$6858 AnimChar68 ; character 68: frames from FramesChar68 (AnimateCells)
$69B0 AnimChar111 ; character 111: each line rotated right (RRC) by the main loop
$6A30 AnimChar127 ; character 127: frames from FramesChar127 (AnimateCells)
$6AB0 AnimChar143 ; character 143: each line rotated left (RLC)
$6E00 AnimChar249 ; character 249: frames from FramesList3 (AnimateRestart)
$6E08 AnimChar250 ; character 250: frames from FramesList2 (AnimateCells2)
$6E18 AnimChar252 ; characters 252-255: AnimFramesA / AnimFramesB on alternate passes (AnimateCells)
$6E38 b CharAttrs 16 ; The attribute of each of the 256 room characters
@res chars/demo.bin
$6F38 b BlockDefs 9 ; The 256 blocks: 3 x 3 character codes each, rows top to bottom
@res blocks/demo.bin
$7838 b RoomMaps 10 ; The room maps: 7 rows of 10 block codes each (70 bytes a room); room n at $7838 + 70n; rooms 0-5
> DrawRoom reads it; TutorRooms $A2A2 plays rooms 4, 1, 0 and 2, and room 2 leads down to room 3.
@res rooms/demo-maps.bin
$79DC b Sprites 16 ; The sprites, pre-shifted: each label is a picture set its owner draws through a frame list (ShiftFrames $AF0E: 8 words, one a pixel phase)
@res sprites/demo.bin
$79DC SpriteKind0 ; kind 0, the foot man (ShiftFrames)
$7BD4 SpriteRexDeath ; Rex's death (DeathAnimation)
$7C1C SpritePoints ; the points sign a kill leaves (ShowPoints $8E4D)
$7F1C SpritePodPower ; a power pod left by an explosion (BlowUp $C49A)
$7FDC SpritePodBig ; a big power pod left by an explosion (BlowUp)
$809C SpritePowerPod ; the power pod's four frames ($809C, $80BC, $80DC, $80FC: AnimatePod)
$829C SpriteLaserA ; a long bullet (MoveBeam)
$82B4 SpriteScanner ; kind 8 (scanner: ScannerTurn, ScannerReset)
$8464 SpriteHudIcons ; the HUD's weapon and bomb icons (DrawHudIcon)
$8504 SpriteHudIcons2 ; the HUD's weapon icons, second row (DrawWeaponIcon)
$8544 SpriteBombPod ; the bomb pod ($FD: BlowUp; kind $7D: InitKind7D)
$8564 SpriteBonusPod ; the bonus pod ($FC: BlowUp; kind $7C: InitKind7C)
$86A4 SpriteKind11 ; kind 11 (launcher, InitKind11)
$86C4 SpriteKind10 ; kind 10 (shooters, InitKind10)
$86E4 SpriteKind6 ; kind 6 (InitKind6)
$8704 SpriteSwingGun ; kind 9 (swing gun), its angles (SwingGunFrames, SwingGun)
$87A4 SpriteLaserB ; a long bullet (MoveBeam)
$887C SpriteJumper ; a walker turned jumper (MaybeJumper)
$88FC SpriteArrow ; the tutor's arrow in room 4 (TutorArrow $8EB8)

@module entry ; The entry, a new demo game
$8A84 c GameEntry ; The code block's entry (USR 35460): DI, keys (ControlXor 0), the tutor's room list from its start (TutorRooms $A2A2), the first room (NextTutorRoom), the tutor reset (TutorReset), then NewGame
> Changed from REX 1's GameEntry $947A (src/game/entry.asm).
> Witness: L1 1 (d1).
$8A95 c NewGame ; A new demo game: the variables reset, 2 lives, 3 bombs, the gun, every weapon panel shown again; the HUD; no menu, no high score
> Changed from REX 1's NewGame $9498 (src/game/entry.asm).
> Witness: L1 7 (d1, demo-cycle).
$8B6A c MainLoop ; Build the room (first the room's tutor: TutorRoom0, 1, 2 or 4), then one pass of play a frame: Rex's moves come from the tutor's input script (TutorStep), the tutor's panels at their frames (TutorPanels), the arrow in room 4 (TutorArrow), SPACE pauses (DemoPause)
> The key tests of part 1 (KeyFire, KeyLeft, ...) read TutorInput $6079 here (TutorKeyFire to TutorKeyShield); no ENTER, H or smart bomb key. The seed is reset at every room (RandomSeed $0313, RandomSeed2 $11, R = 3), so the demo plays the same each time. Room 3 starts the scripted spawn (TutorSpawn3 $A318).
> Witness: L1 12 (d1, demo-cycle).
$8C78 MainRexKeys ; while Rex lives: fire
$8C88 MainRight ; right
$8CA6 MainAnimate ; the animated characters: RRC, RLC, rolls
$8CAB MainRrcLoop ; rotate each line of character 111 right
$8CB5 MainRlcLoop ; rotate each line of character 143 left
$8CDC c MainLoopLeftover ; Leftover: CALL SoundSilence: RET after the main loop's JP; nothing reaches it
> Witness: L1 0 ().

