$A682 MultipleText ; flag, REMOTE DRONE OFFENSIVE SYSTEM ...
$A6E5 SprayText ; flag, MULTI:DIRECTIONAL SPRAY PROJECTILE LAUNCHER ...
$A740 TextSpray3 ; 3 WAY SPRAY
$A74F TextSpray5 ; 5 WAY SPRAY
$A75E TextSpray7 ; 7 WAY SPRAY
$A76D TextSpray4 ; 4 DIRECTIONAL SPRAY
$A784 TextSpray8 ; FULL 8 WAY SPRAY
$A798 TextShield ; YOUR SHIELD CAN BE USED TO DESTROY THE ENEMY AND DEFLECT BULLETS
$A7E5 TextBubbles ; COLLECT THE BUBBLES DROPPED BY THE ENEMY TO INCREASE YOUR WEAPONS ENERGY
$A83A TextBeamPads ; USE BEAM:PADS TO RECORD POSITION
$A862 TextRecharge ; STAND ON DISC TO CHARGE YOUR SHIELD
$A88C TextQuestion ; PICK UP QUESTION MARKS FOR A SKILL BONUS:USE FIRE TO SELECT
$A8D4 TextWalls ; SOME WALLS CAN BE SHOT THROUGH
$A8F9 TextExits ; ARROWS SUGGEST EXITS FROM SCREEN:BUT LOOK FOR SECRET PASSAGES
$A940 TextScanners ; BEWARE OF SCANNERS THEY DETECT ANY MOVEMENT IN THE AREAS SHOWN
$A98E TextFalling ; IF REX FALLS DOWN A SCREEN WITHOUT AN EXIT HE IS FORCED TO BEAM OUT
$A9DE TextTeleport ; AFTER TELEPORTATION REX IS TAKEN TO THE LAST BEAM:PAD
$AA1D TextSmartBombs ; SMART BOMBS CAN KILL ALL THE ENEMIES ON THE SCREEN:EXTRA ONES ARE SOMETIMES LEFT BY THE ENEMY
$AA8A TutorIntro ; YOU ARE ABOUT TO SEE A DEMO OF REX THE DEBUT GAME BY THE LIGHT SPACE:PAUSES DEMO
$AAED TutorPrologue ; FIRST A SHORT PROLOGUE OF HOW REX INFILTRATED THE TOWER THROUGH THE HIDDEN UNDERGROUND RIVER
$AB59 TutorText1 ; NEXT AN EXPLANATION OF THE FIVE WEAPON SYSTEMS REX CAN USE
$AB9E TutorText0 ; YOU HAVE NOW SEEN THE HARDWARE:NOW THE EFFECT IT HAS ON THE ENEMY
$ABE9 TutorText2 ; AND FINALLY A FEW GUIDELINES ON HOW REX CAN MAKE THE BEST OF HIS SUROUNDINGS
$AC42 TutorCredits ; ALL SOFTWARE SOUND AND VISION BY THE LIGHT
$AC86 b PixelMasks 8 ; Leftover: the bit masks $80, $40, ... $01 (part 2's PixelMasks); no code reads them here
$AC8E w ScreenLineTable 8 ; The screen address of each of the 192 pixel lines (PrintChar, PrintDigits, PanelBox, DrawCharBlock)
$ACBE ScreenLines ; line 24 on: the play area's 168 lines, BufferToScreen's list
$AE0E b MirrorTable 16 ; Each byte with its bits reversed: DrawMirrored draws a picture facing left through it
$AF0E w ShiftFrames 8 ; The pictures' frame lists: 8 picture words each, one a pixel phase (X & 7): kind 0, Rex, kinds 1 and 2, 12, 8, Rex jumping and shielded, the swing gun's turn, the hit flash
$AF1E ShieldFrames ; the shield bubble (DrawShield)
$AF2E FramesKind1 ; kinds 1 and 2
$AF3E FramesKind12 ; kind 12
$AF4E FramesKind8 ; kind 8
$AF5E RexFramesJump ; Rex jumping or falling, off a lift (DrawRex)
$AF6E RexFramesWalk ; Rex walking or standing (DrawRex)
$AF7E FramesTurn ; kind 6's turn and kind 7 (SwingGun)
$AF8E FramesHit ; an object hit (HitObject, HitObjectHard)
$AFAE b AnimFramesA 8 ; The frames of the animated characters 252-255 on even passes: 4 x 8 bytes (AnimateCells)
$AFCE AnimFramesB ; on odd passes
$AFEE b RoomObjectLists 16 ; The rooms' object lists (RoomExits' words): a header [spawn sides: bit 7 top, 6 right, 5 left][spawn period] (ReadExits: no spawn kind in DEMO), then [kind][X][Y] records, $FF ends
@res rooms/demo-objects.bin
$B033 b RoomExits 6 ; The exits of the rooms 0-5: up, right, down, left (0 none), then the word of the room's object list
@res rooms/demo-exits.bin
$B057 b TutorScript0 16 ; Room 0's input script (TutorStep): the first count, then [input][count] pairs; input bits low = pressed: 0 fire, 1 up, 2 down (shield), 3 right, 4 left
> 199 pairs, 698 passes. TutorScript1 $B1E7: 495 pairs, 1295 passes; TutorScript2 $B5C7: 309 pairs, 875 passes; TutorScript4 $B833: 327 pairs, 1005 passes. A script plays to its room's end (TutorNextRoom) or a death.
$B1E7 TutorScript1 ; room 1's
$B5C7 TutorScript2 ; room 2's
$B833 TutorScript4 ; room 4's

